WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.140
While a workflow runs, everything its activities save goes through one database session.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.241
The Session Workflows Activities feature adds a task that commits it.

00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:13.740
You'll see that task, and how it works with Fork and Join.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:23.203
A workflow runs inside the shell scope of the request, or the background

00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:25.011
task, that triggers it.

00:00:25.011 --> 00:00:30.560
Every activity of that run receives the same ISession, created once for each scope.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.405
The shell scope commits the session when it ends, and cancels it if

00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:37.032
an exception is thrown.

00:00:37.032 --> 00:00:41.800
Saving a document only records the change, so nothing is committed before then.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.342
The workflow manager follows the same rule.

00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:51.210
It saves the instance through the store, which calls SaveAsync on the session, and never commits.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.786
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for session.

00:00:58.786 --> 00:01:06.430
Under Workflows, Session Workflows Activities provides the session-related activities, and it depends on the Workflows feature.

00:01:06.897 --> 00:01:08.246
Let's enable it.

00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:14.867
The page reloads with a notification, and the feature adds a single activity, Commit Transaction Task.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:22.165
In the workflow designer, the Activities pane lists the task in the Session category.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:28.377
Search for commit, and Commit Transaction appears, described as Commit the current transaction.

00:01:28.848 --> 00:01:35.549
On the canvas, the card shows Commit Transaction Task, with the outcomes Done, Valid and Invalid.

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:40.298
Its editor holds only a title and the retry settings of every task.

00:01:41.898 --> 00:01:43.317
Here is the task.

00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:48.007
When the model state of the current request is invalid, it returns the

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:51.278
outcomes Done and Invalid, and commits nothing.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:56.712
Otherwise it calls SaveChangesAsync, which commits the whole session:

00:01:56.712 --> 00:02:03.269
everything saved in the scope so far, including what the request saved before the workflow started.

00:02:03.269 --> 00:02:07.078
It returns Done and Valid, so Done fires in both cases.

00:02:07.828 --> 00:02:12.497
The model state belongs to the controller or page handling the request.

00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:16.801
When none sets it, the model updater is empty, so the model state

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.348
is valid and the task follows Valid.

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:24.608
The feature registers the task in a startup class limited to it, with

00:02:24.608 --> 00:02:29.358
an empty display driver and view model, because the task has no settings.

00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:38.196
Fork and Join belong to the Workflows module, not to the Session feature.

00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:42.423
A Fork returns one outcome for each name in its Forks setting, and

00:02:42.423 --> 00:02:44.478
each outcome starts a branch.

00:02:45.228 --> 00:02:50.346
The workflow manager pushes the next activity of every outcome onto a stack,

00:02:50.346 --> 00:02:52.343
and runs them in one loop.

00:02:52.343 --> 00:02:56.338
The branches run one after the other, on the same session.

00:02:57.088 --> 00:03:02.137
A Join in WaitAll mode, the default, continues with the outcome Joined once

00:03:02.137 --> 00:03:04.568
every inbound branch has arrived.

00:03:04.568 --> 00:03:10.988
WaitAny continues when any inbound branch has arrived, and drops the waiting activities upstream.

00:03:12.688 --> 00:03:19.249
This workflow, Order handoff, starts with Started By Workflow Event and forks into Billing and Shipping.

00:03:19.249 --> 00:03:22.888
Each branch is a Log task that stands in for real work.

00:03:23.347 --> 00:03:25.521
Both branches lead to a Join.

00:03:25.521 --> 00:03:30.553
After it, Commit Transaction commits the work of both branches at once, and

00:03:30.553 --> 00:03:33.597
its Valid outcome leads to a last Log task.

00:03:34.064 --> 00:03:36.963
Double-click the Fork to open its editor.

00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:41.527
Forks holds comma-separated names, and each name becomes an outcome.

00:03:41.527 --> 00:03:44.364
The Join has a Mode, WaitAll or WaitAny.

00:03:46.064 --> 00:03:47.151
Let's run it.

00:03:47.151 --> 00:03:49.440
Run… starts the published version.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.874
With no input variables, the dialog only needs a click on Run, and the instance finishes.

00:03:55.377 --> 00:03:58.375
Open the instance, and select its Journal tab.

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.834
The records list the activities in the order they ran.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.506
The Join appears twice:

00:04:03.506 --> 00:04:07.427
it waits for the first branch, and continues after the second.

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:12.914
Commit Transaction completes with the outcomes Done and Valid, since nothing added an

00:04:12.914 --> 00:04:14.629
error to the model state.

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:16.399
The last Log task follows.

00:04:20.599 --> 00:04:23.622
Place the task after a Join in WaitAll mode.

00:04:23.622 --> 00:04:28.036
By then, every branch has saved its changes to the session, and one

00:04:28.036 --> 00:04:29.789
commit writes them all.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:34.928
Connect Invalid to the activities that handle a failed validation.

00:04:34.928 --> 00:04:39.986
The admin content editor cancels the session when its model state is invalid.

00:04:39.986 --> 00:04:44.679
The task only skips its own commit, and the scope commits when it ends.

00:04:46.679 --> 00:04:51.751
The Session Workflows Activities feature adds the Commit Transaction task, which commits the

00:04:51.751 --> 00:04:55.063
session in the middle of a run, and it works with Fork and

00:04:55.063 --> 00:04:56.874
Join like any other activity.

00:04:56.874 --> 00:04:58.219
Thanks for watching.

